R"VG(
# medieval10.vg (H-04; the second pass 2026-10-10): the prayer's petition about what has lately happened (`@event ... med.pr 3`: `$e`
# the event, its place, its kind): what happened, then what is asked, each a part with its own turns.

med.pr.fire
  ($e.what=granary) The granary burned at {$e.place}, and the {crop} in it. {med.pr.ask.fire}
  ($e.what=grass|$e.what=forest) The hills burned by {$e.place}, and the {bird} came down into the streets ahead of it. {med.pr.ask.fire}
  ($e.what!=granary $e.what!=grass $e.what!=forest) The fire took {#$e.value|house} at {$e.place}. {med.pr.ask.fire}
  ($e.what=temple) The fire took the house of {god} at {$e.place}. You were not in the roof; be in the ones who rebuild it.
med.pr.ask.fire
  Let the ones who lost them have roofs before {season.next}.
  Keep the sparks out of our {roofs} this time.
  Fill the {vessel} again, and keep them full.
  Give the {med.chr.trades} work at the rebuilding, and good timber.
  Let nobody else's house go the same way, and nobody's child.

med.pr.storm
  ($e.what=hail has:$e.place) The hail broke the {crop} at {$e.place}. {med.pr.ask.storm}
  ($e.what=hail !has:$e.place) The hail broke the {crop} in the low fields. {med.pr.ask.storm}
  ($e.what=wind|$e.what=rain|$e.what=lightning has:$e.place) The storm went over {$e.place} and took {med.pr.took}. {med.pr.ask.storm}
  (!has:$e.place) The storm took {med.pr.took} from us. {med.pr.ask.storm}
  ($e.what=snow) The snow lies on the {herd} in the hills. Bring them down alive.
  ($e.what=dust) The dust has filled {watersrc}. Give us the strength to clean it out again, and the will.
  ($e.what=sea has:$e.place) The sea took the boats at {$e.place}. Give it back what it can give back.
med.pr.took
  what it wanted
  the {roofs} and the fences
  the {fruit} off the trees
  half the {crop2}
  the {herd} that were out
  the old {tree.n} by {holyplace}

med.pr.ask.storm
  Let what is left stand.
  Let it want less next time.
  Mend what it broke, or show us how.
  Send it somewhere with fewer children.

med.pr.pest
  ($e.what=murrain) The {herd} are sick at {$e.place}, and the {med.chr.trades} will not buy them. Spare the rest of them.
  ($e.what=locusts) The locusts came over {$e.place}, and the {crop} went into them. Do not send them twice.
  ($e.what=rats) The rats are in the stores at {$e.place}, in the {vessel} and in the bread. Send us cats, or cleverness.
  ($e.what=wolves) The wolves came down to {$e.place} for the {herd}. Keep the pens shut and the children in.
  ($e.what!=murrain $e.what!=locusts $e.what!=rats $e.what!=wolves) The {pest} are in the {crop} at {$e.place}. Send them somewhere else, and quickly.

med.pr.flood
  {river} came over {$e.place}. {med.pr.ask.flood}
  The water took the low houses at {$e.place}, and the {herd} with them. {med.pr.ask.flood}
med.pr.ask.flood
  Put it back in its bed, and keep it there.
  Dry the houses and the people in them.
  Let the mud be good for the {crop}, since we have so much of it.

med.pr.drought
  No rain for {#$e.value|year}, and the {crop} is dust. One cloud. We are not asking for much.
  {watersrc} is low and the {herd} are thin. Open the sky.
  The {fruit} are dropping green from the trees. Send rain before the rest go.

med.pr.sickness
  {$e.sickness} is at {$e.place}. Take it away, and take it far.
  They are dying at {$e.place} of {$e.sickness}. Spare the children, at least the children.
  {$e.sickness} has come to {$e.place}, and the {med.chr.trades} have shut their doors. Open them again before {festival}.

med.pr.famine
  (has:$e.place) There is hunger at {$e.place}. Fill the {vessel}, or teach us to share what is in ours.
  (!has:$e.place) There is hunger in the land. Fill the {vessel}, or teach us to share what is in ours.
  (!has:$e.place) The children are eating {med.chr.poor}. Let the {crop} come up before they have to eat worse.

med.pr.war
  {$e.war} is on us. Bring the young ones home.
  {$e.war} has taken the young men and the {herd}. Give back what you can; we will bury the rest.

med.pr.battle
  ($e.won=1) We won at {$e.place}. Forgive us the winning; it cost.
  ($e.won=0|$e.won=draw) We lost at {$e.place}. Take the dead, and keep them warm.
  ($e.won=1) The bells are ringing for {$e.place}. Let them ring for the other side's dead as well.

med.pr.quake
  The ground shook at {$e.place}. Hold it still, under us and under them.
  At {$e.place} the walls of {walls.of} came down. Hold up the ones that are left.

med.pr.eruption
  {mountain} burned. Let the ash be good for the {crop}, since it is here.
med.pr.winter
  The cold will not go. Bring the sun back, and the {bird}, and the {crop}.
  The {fuel} is nearly gone and the cold is not. Bring the thaw.

med.pr.harvest
  ($e.harvest=rich) The {crop} came in heavy. Thank you, and keep it from the {pest}.
  ($e.harvest=rich) The {vessel} are full. Make us generous before we are proud.
  ($e.harvest=failed|$e.harvest=poor) The {crop} failed. Let the {fruit} hold out, and the {herd}.
  ($e.harvest=failed|$e.harvest=poor) The {crop} is thin in the {vessel}. Stretch it, the way you stretched it for our mothers.

med.pr.accident
  ($e.what=bridge) The bridge fell at {$e.place}. Hold the ones who fell with it.
  ($e.what=mine) The mine closed over the men at {$e.place}. Find them, wherever they are now.
  ($e.what=ship) The ship went down off {$e.place}. Bring the drowned to a kind shore.
  ($e.what!=bridge $e.what!=mine $e.what!=ship) {#$e.value|soul} died at {$e.place}, and it was nobody's fault. Take them gently.
  ($e.what!=bridge $e.what!=mine $e.what!=ship) The {med.chr.trades} of {$e.place} are burying their own this {season.now}. Give them the strength to dig.

med.pr.omen
  We saw the sign in the sky. Tell us what it means, or tell us not to mind it.
  ($e.omen=eclipse) The sun went out at noon and the {herd} lay down. Do not do that again.
  ($e.omen=comet) The hairy star is in the sky over {$home}. Let it go by without looking at us.
  ($e.omen=redmoon) {moon} went red. If it was a warning, say it plainer.
  ($e.omen=wanderer 3) The wanderer grows over {$home} every year. Send it back where it came from, and leave us our summer.
  ($e.omen=intruder 3) There is a new star, and it is too bright. If it is yours, call it home.
  ($e.omen=dance 3) The second sun is going away from us. Hold it, or hold us.

med.pr.wonder
  ($e.what=calf|$e.what=beast|$e.what=twins) There is a wonder at {$e.place}. Let it be a good one.
  ($e.what=spring|$e.what=rain|$e.what=tree|$e.what=bell) Strange things at {$e.place}. If it is you, say so plainly.
  ($e.what!=calf $e.what!=beast $e.what!=twins $e.what!=spring $e.what!=rain $e.what!=tree $e.what!=bell) There is talk of a wonder at {$e.place}. Keep us from foolishness about it.

med.pr.none
  (2)
  It has been a quiet year at {$home}. Thank you for that.
  Nothing has gone wrong at {$home} this {season.now}, which is how we know you are near.
  The {crop} is in and the {herd} are home, and the {vessel} are full. We have nothing to ask that we did not ask last year.
  No fire, no flood, no sickness at {$home} this {season.now}, and the {herd} all counted. We noticed. Thank you.
)VG"
